  "notes": "USAGE:\nA godan verb (せがむ → せがまない → せがんで). Often used with the passive form せがまれる to describe being on the receiving end of persistent requests, especially from children. The nuance is of repeated, sometimes annoying requests.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- おもちゃをせがむ (to beg for a toy)\n- 〜してとせがむ (to beg someone to do ~)\n- せがまれて{買|か}う (to buy something because one was pestered)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {頼|たの}む: to ask, to request — neutral, not necessarily persistent\n- おねだりする: to beg, to coax — similar but softer, more endearing nuance\n- {強請|ねだ}る: to demand, to pester — can have a stronger, more insistent tone",
